There's no consensus on how Gtk+ should be installed under Win32,
unfortunately. Most likely Slash'EM GTK interface doesn't recognize
the Gtk+ system that you have installed. It may be possible to get
it to recognize it (or you could just install two Gtk+ systems if
you have disk space to spare). If you want help trying to get the
GTK interface to work with the version of Gtk+ you have installed
please log a support request:

